{{- /* Files that belong to SOME machines. Rendered as a template on every
  apply, so a pattern listed here is simply not written on the boxes the
  condition excludes — and is removed if it was written before.

  Preferred over templating the file itself with a {{ "{{ if eq .machine ... }}" }}
  guard, because `mode = "symlink"` means a non-templated file is SYMLINKED
  into this repo and a templated one is not. Turning an existing unit into a
  .tmpl therefore changes its path in ~/.config from a link into ~/.dotfiles to
  a real file — and `systemctl --user enable imapnotify@icloud.service`
  recorded the link's target, so the rename left the instance pointing at a
  path that no longer existed and systemd called it not-found (2026-09-21,
  on the NUC, which is why this file exists). A drop-in that is present or
  absent moves nothing. */ -}}
{{ if ne .machine "nuc" }}
{{/* The mail units must not draw a passphrase prompt on a machine with nobody
     in front of the screen; everywhere else that prompt is how the agent gets
     unlocked at boot. See the drop-ins for the whole story. */}}
.config/systemd/user/imapnotify@.service.d
.config/systemd/user/mail-sync.service.d
{{ end }}

{{/* Python bytecode from the jev skill's scripts importing _jev.py as a
     module. It appears in the source dir the moment a script runs, and
     chezmoi would otherwise try to manage — and prompt about — a cache. */}}
.claude/skills/jev/scripts/__pycache__
